.TH MAKEKEEPER 1 "October 2026" "makekeeper 0.1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
makekeeper \- A safer installer for Makefile-based Linux applications

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makekeeper
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
makekeeper provides a controlled way to install applications that use GNU Make build systems. It tracks all installed files and managed symlinks, enabling safe uninstallation and preventing conflicts with existing installations.

Applications are installed to
.IR /opt/makekeeper/apps/<name>/
and executable symlinks are created in
.IR /usr/local/bin/ .

makekeeper automatically uses pkexec for operations requiring root privileges.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B inspect [PROJECT]
Inspect a project's Makefile and preview installation commands. This shows possible Make targets and a dry-run preview of the installation without actually installing.

.TP
.B install [PACKAGE] [OPTIONS]
Build and install a project. If PACKAGE is a known package name from the catalog, it will be installed from its git repository. Otherwise, use \-\-dir to install from a local directory.

.RS
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dir [PATH]
Install from a specific directory instead of the package catalog.

.TP
.B \-\-name [NAME]
Specify a custom application name. Defaults to the package name or directory name.

.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.

.TP
.B \-\-override
Override an existing installation. This will uninstall the existing version before installing the new one.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed installation output.
.RE
.RE

.TP
.B git [URL] [OPTIONS]
Clone a git repository and install it. The repository is cloned to a cache directory and kept for future updates.

.RS
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-name [NAME]
Specify a custom application name. Defaults to the repository name.

.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.

.TP
.B \-\-override
Override an existing installation. This will uninstall the existing version before installing the new one.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed installation output.
.RE
.RE

.TP
.B update [OPTIONS]
Check for updates to all Git-based installations and rebuild any that have changed on the remote repository.

.RS
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed update output.
.RE
.RE

.TP
.B sync
Download the latest package catalog from the remote server. This is required before using package-based installation or search.

.TP
.B search [QUERY]
Search the package catalog for applications matching your query. Searches across package names, descriptions, categories, and URLs.

.TP
.B fetch
Show the count of installed packages and Git-tracked packages.

.TP
.B list
List all registered applications with file and symlink counts.

.TP
.B info [NAME]
Display detailed information about an installed application, including source, prefix, installed files, and managed symlinks.

.TP
.B uninstall [NAME] [OPTIONS]
Remove tracked files and managed executable symlinks. Only unchanged files are removed; modified files are preserved for manual review.

.RS
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.

.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed removal output.
.RE
.RE

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.

.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information.

.SH EXAMPLES

Sync package catalog:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper sync
.fi
.RE

Search for packages:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper search terminal
.fi
.RE

Install from package catalog:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper install neofetch
.fi
.RE

Install from directory:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper install --dir /path/to/project
.fi
.RE

Install with a custom name:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper install --dir /path/to/project --name myapp
.fi
.RE

Install from a git repository:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper git https://github.com/user/project
.fi
.RE

Update Git-based installations:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper update
.fi
.RE

Inspect before installing:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper inspect /path/to/project
.fi
.RE

List installed applications:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper list
.fi
.RE

View installation details:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper info myapp
.fi
.RE

Uninstall an application:
.RS
.PP
.nf
makekeeper uninstall myapp
.fi
.RE

.SH FILES

.TP
.I /opt/makekeeper/apps/<name>/
Installation prefix for applications.

.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/
Directory where executable symlinks are created.

.TP
.I /var/lib/makekeeper/<name>.json
Installation records tracking files and symlinks.

.SH SECURITY

makekeeper automatically uses pkexec for operations requiring root privileges. Makefiles can execute arbitrary code; only install projects you trust. Always inspect a project with makekeeper inspect before installing. The make install step is not sandboxed.

.SH REQUIREMENTS

\- Linux system
.br
\- GNU Make
.br
\- Rust toolchain (for building makekeeper)
.br
\- Root/sudo access for installation and management

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR make (1)

.SH AUTHOR
makekeeper v0.1.0
